.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Vt OSSL_IETF_ATTR_SYNTAX
is an opaque structure that represents the IetfAttrSyntax type defined
in RFC 5755 (Section 4.4) for use as an AttributeValue.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_IETF_ATTR_SYNTAX_get0_policyAuthority
and
.Fn OSSL_IETF_ATTR_SYNTAX_set0_policyAuthority
get and set the policyAuthority field of the structure.
Both routines act on internal pointers of the structure and must not be
freed by the application.
.Pp
An
.Vt OSSL_IETF_ATTR_SYNTAX
object also holds a sequence of values.
.Fn OSSL_IETF_ATTR_SYNTAX_get_value_num
returns the number of values in the sequence.
.Fn OSSL_IETF_ATTR_SYNTAX_add1_value ,
adds a copy of
.Fa data
of a specified
.Fa type
to the sequence.
The caller should free the
.Fa data
after use.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_IETF_ATTR_SYNTAX_get0_value
will return the value and a specific index
.Fa ind
in the sequence or NULL on error.
If
.Fa type
is not NULL, the type of the value will be written to this location.
.Pp
The
.Fa type
of the values stored in the
.Vt OSSL_IETF_ATTR_SYNTAX
value sequence is one of the following:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It OSSL_IETFAS_OCTETS
A pointer to an ASN1_OCTET_STRING
.It OSSL_IETFAS_OID
A pointer to an ASN1_OBJECT
.It OSSL_IETFAS_STRING
A pointer to an ASN1_UTF8STRING
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn OSSL_IETF_ATTR_SYNTAX_get0_policyAuthority
returns an pointer to a
.Vt GENERAL_NAMES
structure or
.Dv NULL
if the policy authority has not been set.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_IETF_ATTR_SYNTAX_get_value_num
returns the number of entries in the value sequence or -1 on error.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_IETF_ATTR_SYNTAX_get0_value
returns a pointer to the value at the given index or NULL if the index
is out of range.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_IETF_ATTR_SYNTAX_add1_value
returns 1 on success and 0 on failure.
